te biomarkers\"\n\n\n- Section 10.7 \"Standardization and validation imperatives\" explicitly states: \"A significant technical challenge in microbiome-metabolite research is the absence of standardized protocols for metabolomic analysis and multi-omics integration\"\n\n**Gap Status Assessment:**\nThe paper does NOT provide:\n- Specific standardized measurement protocols for inosine or SCFAs\n- Reference ranges for absolute concentrations\n- Consensus guidelines or statements\n\nThe paper DOES indicate:\n- This is an unresolved challenge in the field\n- Multiple analytical platforms exist (LC-MS, GC-MS, NMR) but lack standardization\n- Standardization is identified as a key research priority\n\n**Material Usefulness:**\n- **Direct:** The paper directly addresses the standardization gap by confirming its existence and documenting current methodological limitations\n- **Supporting:** Provides context on available analytical techniques and their variability, which helps explain why consensus standards haven't emerged yet\n- **None:** The paper doesn't offer actionable protocols or reference values that would resolve the gap\n\n**Status:** partial (the gap remains unresolved, but the paper confirms this and provides supporting context)\n\n**Material_usefulness:** supporting (the paper helps understand WHY the gap exists and what platforms are being used, but doesn't provide the actual standardized protocols requested)\n\nLet me structure the JSON response properly.",
